<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48283" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Thyrē</span></b> ,
		ēs, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Θύρη,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a little town in
				the Peloponnesus</i>, <i>the possession of which
				was contested by the Argives and the
			Lacedæmonians</i>, <i><span class="en">Stat. Th. 4,
				48</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Thy-rĕātis</span></b> ,
				ĭdis, <i>adj. f.</i>,
				<i>Thyreatic</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">terra,</span>”
				<i>the region of Thyre</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. F.
					2, 663</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
